          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Pierre\",\"addressee\":\"Hélène\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Je vous aime!\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Its later characterization as a lie bears on sincerity, not on its clear avowal form and force at the time.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"later_1\",\"quotation\":\"он сказал эти невыходившие из него слова: «Je vous aime»\"},{\"block_id\":\"later_1\",\"quotation\":\"зачем я ей сказал этот: «Je vous aime», которое было ложь и еще хуже чем ложь\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.84,\"reason\":\"In this occurrence, the declaration is not a separate explicit marriage proposal: Prince Vasiliy's blessing and the social treatment of Pierre and Hélène as engaged have already established that setting. Nevertheless, Pierre understands that a final conventional utterance is required, and “Je vous aime” supplies it, affirming his acceptance of the fiancé and prospective-husband role into which the scene has placed him. It therefore substantially ratifies a marital bond, though the commitment's terms are only implicit.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты и смотрел на ее поднимающуюся и опускающуюся прекрасную грудь.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он, но никак не мог вспомнить, чтò такое именно говорят в этих случаях.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Через полтора месяца он был обвенчан\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"reason\":\"The expression is not represented as a spontaneous or reflex-like discharge of affect. Pierre deliberately recalls and produces the socially expected formula, and its poor sound makes him self-conscious.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях; но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"No substantial residual force is needed beyond the direct avowal and its contextual ratification of the marital bond. The utterance's conventionality and awkwardness qualify those modes rather than establishing another core function.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Pierre and Hélène have been left alone after Prince Vasiliy's public blessing has caused them to be treated as an engaged couple. After Hélène kisses him, Pierre recalls the expected words for such an occasion and tells her, “Je vous aime!”\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression implicitly ratifies Pierre's position as Hélène's fiancé and prospective husband rather than independently spelling out or initiating a marriage proposal. Prince Vasiliy's blessing is a separate speech act, but it creates the immediate setting in which Pierre regards the love declaration as the required final formula. Hélène gives no recorded verbal response after the target; her preceding kiss and their marriage a month and a half later provide practical uptake. Sincerity is doubtful: Pierre thinks immediately that he loves her, but later calls the declaration a lie and says he never loved her.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passages are recognisable as Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace. The classification uses only the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence gives strong access to Pierre's immediate thoughts and later retrospective judgment, but these conflict concerning actual affection. It does not record Hélène's verbal response to the focal utterance or specify mutually negotiated terms of the marital undertaking.\"}"
        }
      ],
